1
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:08,400
In five seconds, a solar storm as strong as 1859 hits Earth.

2
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,800
Why is the sky red?

3
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:16,440
Seventeen hours ago, the Sun threw billions of tons of plasma straight at us.

4
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:21,500
In 1859, auroras like this were seen as far south as Cuba.

5
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,300
It's moving...

6
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:29,080
Gold miners in the Rocky Mountains woke up and started making breakfast. They thought it was morning.

7
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:31,200
What was that?

8
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:35,900
Back then, telegraph wires threw sparks and set paper on fire.

9
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:41,660
Today, power lines act like giant antennas. The current burns out transformers.

10
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,520
No signal...

11
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:56,520
In 2012, a storm this big crossed Earth's orbit. It missed us by nine days.

12
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,300
It will happen again.

13
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:01,160
We just don't know when.
